Z||000004||zeusrekning||03-08-2001||09:11 AM||||Ok,I feel kind of offended. I am the one that sends out the emails asking who can make it. I know alot of people have bad memories and a lot of people are interested. I planned this Along time ago so no one could say the didn't have notice.I agree Bob is doing a great job getting people together. If hickory is close i'll try to make it. I need to have some notice before i can go out of town most of the time.<BR>I feel mabey bob assumes i'm upset because he does alot of meets. Bob, if you can organize some in SC that would be great. I'm not entering a popularity contest. I met joel and alot of other fiero guys at williamsburg last year. ME, Joel ,Motorhead, and i believe you also Brian , were discussing a fiero club for the Carolinas.I jsut wanted a way to know who my fiero neighbors are and if i decide to go to the beach,moutains,race in rockingham, or any where else in SC or NC i could meet up with them.<P>But Bob I think it would be great for you to organize some stuff in SC if possible. The olny thing that makes me feel bad about all of your get togethers is that i can't attend, since seeing fieros is why i started CFA, and why i frequent this forum.<BR>Brian, You said "you guys'could show up to."<BR>Made it sound like you were refering to me ..<BR>if not, thats cool, if so,cool still. I'll check my map. I would really like to come. <BR>Would i be accepted if i drove my 'Vette ???<P>(hope no  one takes offense)||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||03-08-2001||08:29 PM||||no, i certainly didn't intend to offend anyone, much less pick on you, zeus.<P>i was just merely pointing out that everytime Bob has an anouncement about a saturday luncheon, galen/rae/ mrx  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  always says some comment that is kinda powty.  <P>it has been stated, that these are unoficial (read: not club oriented) get togethers, located around the area, with help from local people to find a conveinent place to meet.  that's all they are.  i believe that i speak for at least two people, in saying that we aren't interested in any kind of formal club... been there done that b4.<P>anyway, i am always willing to go to something withing a two hour drive (honestly, my car hasn't been any further than that in 5 years), weather and little lady permiting!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>hoop||||reg||1
